# Azerbaijani leads with the daypart adverbial exactly as Turkish does:
# "axşam saat səkkizdə" is the ordinary way to say eight in the evening. The
# explanatory dictionary glosses "saat" as vaxt, çağ, an, zaman and
# illustrates it with "axşam saatlarında" -- the daypart word standing before
# the hour noun (Azərbaycan dilinin izahlı lüğəti, s.v. "saat").
axşam
# "gecə" (night) scopes the clock to the PM half the same way -- "gecə saat
# doqquz" is nine at night, 21:00 (Azərbaycan dilinin izahlı lüğəti, s.v.
# "gecə").
gecə
